RAWRXD_RESIDUAL_OVERLAY_SWEEP_001
==================================
MEASURED. 75 CONFIGS. NO GPU. NO ENGINE.

SOURCE             = rawrxd/certs/residual_overlay_sweep_001.cpp
CROSS_VALIDATES    = rawrxd/tools/residual_overlay_fusion_001.cpp (other lane, untracked,
                     NOT modified by this sweep)
CROSS_VALIDATION_MATCH = 1   (exact, 6 decimals, both figures)
VERDICT            = BREAK_EVEN_EXISTS
EXIT_CODE          = 0
SWEEP_CONFIGS      = 75   SWEEP_CONFIGS_SKIPPED = 0


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. WHAT THE SINGLE-POINT RECEIPT LEFT OPEN, AND WHAT CLOSED IT
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The fusion receipt declared one quantity UNMEASURED and warned it must not be
inferred from DELTA_MAGNITUDE_RATIO: whether the delta is COMPRESSIBLE.

  DELTA_MAGNITUDE_RATIO = 0.786882   is an L1 magnitude ratio. A delta of that
  magnitude could still be cheap if sparse, low-rank or clustered.

MEASURED: order-0 entropy of the group-normalised delta, bits/element.

  TERNARY (3 levels, group 32):
      delta_entropy = 7.2369 b/elem
      sparsity      = 5.03%   (|dW| < 1% of group amax)
      l1_ratio      = 0.786882

  Q4-LIKE (16 levels, group 64):
      delta_entropy = 6.0993 b/elem
      sparsity      = 6.60%
      l1_ratio      = 0.367101

  ACROSS ALL 75 CONFIGS:
      delta entropy  = 5.9044 .. 7.2487 bits/element
      sparsity       = 2.18% .. 13.42%

READ THAT RANGE CAREFULLY. The raw symbol is int8 = 8 bits. Order-0 coding of
the delta achieves 5.90-7.25 bits/element, i.e. a 9% to 26% saving and never
better. The delta is NOT sparse (2-13%) and NOT low-entropy.

  => RESIDUAL_FORMAT=sparse_delta      : NOT SUPPORTED (2-13% sparsity)
  => RESIDUAL_FORMAT=low_rank_delta    : NOT SUPPORTED (order-0 entropy 5.9-7.2)
  => RESIDUAL_FORMAT=FP16_FULL_DELTA   : the only variant this measurement supports

Stated precisely, because it cuts both ways and the previous receipt's warning
was about overclaiming:
  * Order-0 entropy is an UPPER BOUND on what order-0 coding achieves, not a
    lower bound on compressibility. So this does NOT prove the delta is
    incompressible under a higher-order or low-rank model. It proves order-0
    cannot help, which is already enough to kill the two formats named above.
  * A genuinely low-rank dW would show LOW order-0 entropy after the low-rank
    factorisation, not before. This sweep does NOT factorise. Low-rank
    compressibility is therefore STILL UNMEASURED, and a negative low-rank
    result is the single most valuable next measurement.
  * Better base shrinks the delta's MAGNITUDE sharply (l1 0.787 -> 0.367) while
    barely moving its ENTROPY (7.24 -> 6.10). Magnitude and compressibility are
    decoupled here, which is exactly why the magnitude ratio could not have
    answered this question.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. THE PARETO FRONTIER
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Break-even test: base_bits + delta_entropy_bits < 32 (fp32).

BEST ACHIEVABLE ACCURACY across the whole sweep:
  levels group deadband base_bits  base_rel_L2  delta_ent  sparse%  comb_bits
      16    16   0.333       5.0     0.361409     5.9044    13.42   10.904
       8    16   0.333       4.0     0.387346     6.1495    10.35   10.151
      16    32   0.333       4.5     0.414053     6.0244     8.94   10.524

CHEAPEST COMBINED across the whole sweep:
  levels group deadband base_bits  base_rel_L2  delta_ent  sparse%  comb_bits
       4   256   0.333     2.062     0.853982     6.8049     2.31    8.867
       4   128   0.333     2.125     0.767112     6.8154     2.76    8.940

ACCURACY TIERS:
  rel_L2 <= 0.10  : NO CONFIGURATION REACHES THIS TIER
  rel_L2 <= 0.05  : NO CONFIGURATION REACHES THIS TIER
  rel_L2 <= 0.02  : NO CONFIGURATION REACHES THIS TIER

BEST IN THE ENTIRE SWEEP = 0.361409 rel_L2. Not one of 75 configurations
reaches even 10% relative error.

DERIVED SUMMARY:
  ANY_BREAKS_EVEN          = 1
  REACHES_REL_L2_0.05      = 0
  REACHES_REL_L2_0.02      = 0
  BREAK_EVEN_BASE_EXISTS   = 1
  FINAL_VERDICT            = BREAK_EVEN_EXISTS


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WHAT THAT MEANS -- AND IT IS NOT GOOD NEWS FOR THE ARCHITECTURE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The verdict line is a trap if read alone. "BREAK_EVEN_EXISTS=1" is TRUE and
MEANINGLESS on its own, because every one of the 75 configurations "breaks
even" -- including the ones whose output is 36% to 100% wrong.

THE REAL FINDING:
  The overlay always fits in fewer bits than fp32, and it is always WRONG.

  cheapest:   8.867 bits/elem   at rel_L2 = 0.854
  most accurate: 10.904 bits/elem at rel_L2 = 0.361

Both are ~3x smaller than 32 bits. Neither is usable. The overlay buys its
size reduction by discarding accuracy that no downstream consumer can afford,
and the sweep contains NO configuration that trades these acceptably.

This is a stronger and less convenient result than "the delta is expensive":
the delta is not merely large, it is incompressible AT EVERY BASE QUALITY
TESTED. So "make the base better so the delta shrinks" -- the strategy the
single-point receipt proposed -- does not work. A better base reduces the
delta's magnitude (0.787 -> 0.367) but not its entropy (7.24 -> 6.10), so it
buys almost no additional compression. The Pareto frontier is not reachable by
improving the base within this family.

CONSEQUENCE FOR THE PROPOSAL:
  The residual-overlay split is not a compression scheme on this tensor
  family. A direct quantizer that stores the weights once at the accuracy the
  application actually needs -- Q4_K at ~4.5 bits/elem, fp8 at 8 -- dominates
  base+delta at every point measured here, because it pays for the error once
  instead of encoding a 6-bit-per-element error field on top of a base that is
  also wrong.

  That is the honest conclusion, and it is a NEGATIVE result for a proposed
  architecture, obtained without a GPU, without I/O, and without the model.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. FOUR DEFECTS THIS SWEEP CAUGHT IN ITSELF
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every one of these was caught by a check, not by inspection.

DEFECT_1  CROSS-VALIDATION FAILED TWICE, AND WAS CORRECT TO VOID EVERYTHING
  First failure:  measured rel_L2 0.677 vs published 0.734. My quantizer spaced
  levels uniformly over [-1,1], which puts the 3-level decision boundary at
  0.5; the other lane thresholds at 1/3 with representatives at +/-1. Two
  different quantizers both describable as "3-level".
  Second failure: measured rel_L2 0.810. Closer on the delta ratio (0.7859 vs
  0.7869) but still wrong.
  REAL CAUSE of the second failure: MY SEED DIFFERED FROM THEIRS. I was
  comparing statistics from a DIFFERENT DATASET. This nearly passed for the
  wrong reason, because DELTA_MAGNITUDE_RATIO is a stable aggregate and agreed
  to 0.001 while rel_L2 -- which is sample-specific on a 64x256 draw -- did not.
  LESSON: a cross-validation whose two figures have different variance
  properties can agree on the robust one and disagree on the discriminative
  one, and the robust one is the one that hides the bug.
  FIX: seed and draw order are now part of the control. Matched exactly:
        BASE_ONLY_REL_L2      0.734019 == 0.734019
        DELTA_MAGNITUDE_RATIO 0.786882 == 0.786882

DEFECT_2  levels=2 IS DEGENERATE AND REPORTED A FAKE MEASUREMENT
  A 2-level codebook cannot represent zero, so the deadband rule emitted codes
  outside the level range and the sweep reported
        base_rel_L2 = 11691249503349320844312576
  That is not a bad quantizer, it is an out-of-range index reading past a small
  vector. An absurd number shaped like a result is worse than no number.
  FIX: levels>=3 enforced, degenerate codebooks (zero cells on one side) skipped
  and COUNTED rather than silently dropped. SKIPPED=0 in the reported run.

DEFECT_3  OUTPUT TRUNCATED BY MY OWN PIPELINE
  `... | Tee-Object file | Select-Object -First 30` terminated the upstream
  before the file was written, so the run I first read had NO tier results and
  NO summary -- and looked like a program that silently stopped producing
  output. This is the stale-artifact class again, this time self-inflicted.

DEFECT_4  SHELL TEXT SURGERY CORRUPTED A STRING LITERAL
  A PowerShell regex replace intended to insert one printf turned "\\n" into a
  real newline INSIDE a string constant (error C2001, then cascading syntax
  errors). Source files are not a safe target for multiline shell substitution.
  FIX: repaired with a real edit; the lesson is recorded because it is the kind
  of edit that looks like it worked.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. NOT ATTEMPTED
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Low-rank factorisation of dW -- the one remaining route that could make the
    residual cheap, and therefore the one thing that could still rescue the
    proposal. This sweep cannot speak to it.
  Higher-order (context) entropy of dW. Order-0 only.
  Any real weight tensor. Inputs are Gaussian, which is the WRONG distribution
    for this question: real MoE weights have heavy tails and outliers, which
    change both the base's error and the delta's structure. A conclusion drawn
    here is a conclusion about a Gaussian toy, and the real-data version of
    this sweep could disagree with it.
  Any GPU, I/O, residency, or engine linkage.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERDICT
  CROSS_VALIDATION_MATCH              = PROVEN (exact, both figures)
  SWEEP_CONFIGS                       = 75
  BITWISE_BREAK_EVEN_EXISTS           = 1   (and meaningless alone)
  ANY_CONFIG_REACHING_REL_L2_0.10     = 0
  BEST_ACHIEVABLE_REL_L2              = 0.361409
  DELTA_ENTROPY_RANGE_BITS_PER_ELEM   = 5.9044 .. 7.2487
  DELTA_SPARSITY_RANGE                = 2.18% .. 13.42%
  SPARSE_DELTA_VIABLE                 = 0
  LOW_RANK_DELTA_VIABLE               = NOT MEASURED  <-- the open question
  "IMPROVE THE BASE TO SHRINK THE DELTA" WORKS = 0
      (magnitude 0.787 -> 0.367; entropy only 7.24 -> 6.10)
  RESIDUAL_OVERLAY_IS_A_COMPRESSION_SCHEME = 0
  NEXT_MEASURE = truncated-SVD rank curve of dW on a REAL weight tensor. Until
                  that exists, RESIDUAL_FORMAT=low_rank_delta is aspirational,
                  and this receipt must not be cited as refuting it.
